    "story": "Nobody's grandfather remembers it sharp. He remembers the heat of it standing at the crossing, the way the light went strange, the whistle arriving from inside his own chest. Memory keeps the engine and loses the edges. It keeps her enormous and near, the station house leaning in like family, the smoke gone the color of the sky in August. Ask him for details and he'll laugh. It wasn't details. It was this, exactly this, and then he goes quiet, because this is the part with no words assigned to it.",
