    "story": "Passengers get the varnish and the timetables. Freight gets the fog. Sixteen comes out of the mist with a string of hoppers behind her, doing the unglamorous work the railroad was actually built for: coal out, goods in, the valley's living carried in open cars. The fog takes the edges off everything except the plume, which drags behind her like the signature on a letter the whole town will read by noon. Nobody waves at a freight. She doesn't take it personally. The work was never the applause.",
