    "story": "There's nothing in the timetable about this little crossing, no station, no name on the map. But the grade on the far side doesn't care about the map, so she takes the culvert at everything she has: twice the plume, twice the noise, the whole machine leaning into a hill most drivers wouldn't slow down for. That's the thing about Sixteen. She doesn't know how to give a crossing less than all of it. The men who built her in 1916 put the capacity in. She just declines to leave any of it unused.",
