    "story": "Ask about her now and this is how she comes back: not in the full dark, but in the brown of old paper, the edges gone soft, the one lit eye smaller than it was. Memory is a merciful editor. It keeps the shape of the fear and lets the fear itself drain out, until what's left is almost fondness. Almost. The men who met her on the night road would tell you the fondness is a lie the years tell. Then they'd look at this picture a moment longer than they meant to.",
    "notes": "The same frame as Creature of the darkness., offered in sepia, and the pairing is the lesson: nothing in the composition has changed, yet the apparition has become a memory. Where the black and white master withholds in darkness, this treatment warms and softens, the white border and aged tonality presenting the image as a found artifact from the railroad's own century. Collectors hang the two together to show visitors what finish alone can do to a story, and to ask which version is true.",
