    "story": "No locomotive in this one. Just the open platform of the last car, a railing, a lantern, and the track unwinding behind into country the train has already finished with. Everybody photographs the engine. Nobody rides facing backward, watching the railroad give the world back piece by piece: the crossing they just made, the field already emptying of sound. The last car doesn't go anywhere first. It arrives last, having seen everything twice: once coming, once going. There's a lesson in that nobody asked for.",
    "notes": "The series' only frame with no engine at all, and it earns its place by inversion: the subject is departure itself, the railroad seen from the one seat that faces where you've been. The platform's ironwork, riveted railing, hanging lantern, worn deck boards, is rendered in crisp tonal detail at the top of the frame, while the track below softens into distance. In a collection dominated by power and plume, this quiet piece is the one that explains the rest: what the machine was FOR was the leaving and the looking back.",
